tasks.descriptionMarkdown:
Implement design `api-evolution`:

- `#[non_exhaustive]` on the listed types, with `RuntimeLimits` `with_*` setters;
- `DtcgRuntime::limits()` and a redacted `Debug`;
- `DtcgError::UnresolvedReference`, replacing every `Projection` that resolution raises (`resolver.rs` missing alias targets, `effective_group_type`, `extension_path`), plus its diagnostic code;
- `Clone` and `PartialEq` on `DtcgError`;
- closing backticks in the `InvalidResourceId`/`InvalidPointer` messages;
- public `Resolution::map`, `is_ready`, `is_missing` and `missing` (remove the private `ResolutionMap` trait);
- `SourceOccurrence::resource()`;
- `DtcgRuntime::replace_envelope`;
- canonical (sorted-key) value serialization in the fingerprint, and canonical equality for `ResolvedTokens`;
- the corrected `ModifierAxis` and `diagnostics` module docs.

**Existing tests.** Update the tests that pinned old behavior: the `RuntimeLimits` literals in `lazy_catalog` and `source_inspection`, and the `Projection` expectations in `dtcg_2025_10_conformance`.

**New test group.** Cover `api_foundations` with a redaction test for the `Debug` output and an envelope-replacement round trip.

Implement designs `bounded-work` (reference part) and `pointer-syntax`:

- **Hop accounting.** One hop counter covers token aliases, token-target pointers and document pointers, in `resolve_value`, `resolve_json_reference*` and `collect_token_dependencies`.
- **Memoization.** Memoize document pointers keyed by (document identity, pointer), with the same key for cycle detection. Pop a pointer before its sibling overrides are resolved.
- **Value size.** `RuntimeLimits::max_value_nodes` with `with_max_value_nodes`. Memo entries carry node counts, which are checked before materializing.
- **`max_alias_depth`** counts hops only, so a limit of 0 allows literal tokens.
- **Pointer parsing.** One RFC 6901 URI-fragment parser (percent-decoding, strict array indexes) serves resource fragments and `$ref`s. Token-target and document traversal share one segment walker.

**Probes to turn into tests** (from the 2026-10-06 audit):
- the 100k-hop chain, run on a spawned thread with a 1 MiB stack;
- 40-level pointer fan-out, expected to hit `LimitExceeded { kind: "value nodes" }`;
- a cross-source pointer cycle false positive in both orders;
- a sibling override pointing at its own target;
- `+1`, `01` and `-1` indexes;
- `%20` fragments.

Implement design `bounded-work` (expansion part):

- `RuntimeLimits::max_tokens` (default 100,000, with a `with_max_tokens` setter), checked whenever `flatten_group` emits a token;
- `effective_group_type` and `$extends` targets memoized by group path, with `HashSet` cycle tracking;
- every discovery expansion step (each set reference, local reference and nested resolver) counted against `max_documents` in `Discovery::append_source` and `expand`.

The probes for 30-level `$extends` doubling, a 400-group linear chain, and 12-level empty-set fan-out each run through `resolve`, `validate_complete` and `inspect_source`.

Implement design `format-structure` in `flatten_group`:

- token objects must have no non-`$` members, no `$root`, and not both `$value` and `$ref`;
- `$root` must be a token;
- there is no token-level `$ref` at a source root;
- names are non-empty;
- `$description` is a string, `$deprecated` a boolean or string, and `$extensions` an object (on tokens, groups and roots).

**Existing tests.** Update any test that relied on silently ignored children.

**Ratchet.** Remove these fixtures from `KNOWN_GAPS`: `group/both-value-and-children`, the four `metadata/*` fixtures, and `references/ref-and-value-both-present`.

Implement design `type-order`:

- record each token's own type and its group-inherited type separately during flattening;
- in `resolve_token`, apply own → whole-reference target → group → error, with token-level `$ref` included;
- report `reference type mismatch` when an own type differs from the whole-reference target's type.

Cover with the `type_determination` group: an alias in a differently typed group, a token-level `$ref` to a non-token location that inherits the group type, and a `fontWeight` → `number` mismatch.

Implement design `reference-positions`:

- thread a position context through `resolve_value`;
- add the static table of (composite type, member) → expected type, including array elements;
- reject curly-brace strings outside allowed positions;
- type-check curly-brace targets at member positions.

**Positive fixtures.** Every positive corpus reference fixture must keep passing.

**Ratchet.** Remove the four `*-curly-brace-in-subvalue` fixtures from `KNOWN_GAPS`.

**Docs.** The `fontFamily` array-alias example in `docs/04-aliases-and-references.md` becomes invalid. Leave the docs for `task-docs`, but note it in the commit.

Implement design `merged-structure`:

- fold discovery's terminal occurrences into a merged tree, with per-key group properties, whole-token replacement, a provenance map and definition sequence numbers;
- report collision errors;
- flatten the merged tree once, with type inheritance and dependency-ordered `$extends` on the merged tree (keeping the `bounded-work` memoization and limits);
- resolve pointers against the merged tree;
- fold preview occurrences in last.

**Existing tests.** The groups named in `merge.compatibility` must keep passing, changed only where an expectation intentionally moves. Record each change in the commit.

**Docs example.** The overlay example from `docs/06-resolvers-and-modifiers.md` that previously failed becomes a test case.

Implement design `metadata-model`:

- `Deprecation`;
- `ResolvedToken::description` and `deprecated`;
- `ResolvedGroup` with `ResolvedTokens::group` and `groups`;
- deprecation inheritance with `false` overrides, evaluated on the merged tree;
- `$extends`-produced groups carrying the extended group's properties.

The fingerprint stays metadata-neutral.

Implement design `resolver-validation` (validation part).

**Rules:**
- allowed-member tables for the root, sets, modifiers and inline steps;
- root `$extensions` rejected, `$defs` and `$schema` allowed;
- an empty `resolutionOrder` rejected;
- single-context modifiers rejected.

**Scope.** The rules apply to nested resolvers and envelope `data`.

**Existing tests.** `alias_overlay` and other tests that use single-context modifiers or extra resolver members change only where the new rules require. Record each change.

**Ratchet.** Remove the five resolver fixtures from `KNOWN_GAPS`. `KNOWN_GAPS` must then be empty, which completes `corpus.complete`; `check-corpus-complete` verifies it.

Implement design `resolver-validation` (consistency part):

- an `effective_steps` function, used by discovery, input validation, `modifiers()` and `normalize_selection`, that honors `$ref` sibling overrides;
- duplicate modifier names and unnamed inline modifiers rejected consistently;
- token-document roots with a `modifiers` group report no axes;
- `source_references` walks reference objects that target resolvers through their overlaid `sets` and `modifiers`.

Turn the planning and audit probes into tests: a step `default` override with and without a root default, a root and inline modifier with the same name, and an override-site listing.

Implement design `input-semantics`:

- exact-then-case-folded matching, with ambiguity errors and declared spellings in `normalize_selection`;
- unknown-key validation against the union of the modifiers declared by reached resolvers, after discovery;
- per-resolver application of inputs and defaults;
- inputs ignored when no modifiers are declared;
- `selection_from_json` and `DtcgError::InvalidInput`.

**Existing tests.** `resolver_2025_10` input expectations change only where case-insensitivity or the scope rule requires it.

Implement design `typed-values`:

- the `values` module types, `TypedValue` and `ResolvedToken::typed`;
- `FromDtcgValue` impls;
- the alpha default, gradient clamping, the font-weight keyword table, the shadow layer and `inset` defaults, and `Dimension::to_px`;
- the extension types gated by `ValueExtensions`;
- `f32` overflow reported as an error.

The tests cover every type with at least one positive corpus fixture value.

Implement design `derive-design` in `dtcg_runtime_derive`:

- strict attribute models with spanned errors;
- fully qualified generated paths and `unraw()` identifiers;
- `Option<T>` leaf fields;
- per-field bounds;
- `trybuild` as a dev-dependency (declared once in `[workspace.dependencies]`), with `tests/compile_fail.rs` and `tests/ui/*.rs` plus `.stderr` snapshots;
- the misnamed `tests/trybuild.rs` renamed to `tests/derive_shapes.rs`.

**Unchanged.** `rest` stays a `Default` placeholder.

**Tests.** The runtime-behavior cases go in `tests/derive_hardening.rs`.

Implement design `docs-as-tests`: `#[cfg(doctest)]` modules in `lib.rs` that include the README and every `docs/*.md` chapter.

**Update the README and chapters 1–14** for every behavior change in this epic. Chapter 12 states the official corpus result, the conformance tiers and every implementation-defined choice.

**Remove outdated passages:**
- the old surprises (type not inherited by overrides, `$extends` limited to one source, the nested-selection constraint, `$schema` rejection);
- the old `Projection` usage for alias errors;
- fontFamily array aliases;
- default-on RayX extensions;
- `RuntimeLimits` literals.

Every Rust example must compile under the doctest check.
